[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3014215193","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108051#issuecomment-3014215193","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108051","id":3014215193,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6zqUYZ","user":{"login":"RoyBerardo","id":32561682,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTYxNjgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32561682?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo","html_url":"https://github.com/RoyBerardo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-27T19:53:14Z","updated_at":"2025-06-27T19:53:14Z","body":"Had a realization of something, tested to confirm that it does happen. If doppler tracking is disabled on the listener but enabled on a stream player, doppler will still be heard. I'm on the fence on if this is a bug or not, since the doppler setting enables _tracking_, not doppler itself. If this IS a bug, should I tackle that in this PR as well? To add, the camera currently exhibits this behavior, so fixing this bug would fix it for both listeners and cameras.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3014215193/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3043737168","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108051#issuecomment-3043737168","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108051","id":3043737168,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61a75Q","user":{"login":"RoyBerardo","id":32561682,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTYxNjgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32561682?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo","html_url":"https://github.com/RoyBerardo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-07T07:09:25Z","updated_at":"2025-07-07T07:09:25Z","body":"> Had a realization of something, tested to confirm that it does happen. If doppler tracking is disabled on the listener but enabled on a stream player, doppler will still be heard. I'm on the fence on if this is a bug or not, since the doppler setting enables tracking, not doppler itself. If this IS a bug, should I tackle that in this PR as well? To add, the camera currently exhibits this behavior, so fixing this bug would fix it for both listeners and cameras.\r\n\r\nI've decided to convert this PR to a draft for now, since I feel this is an important topic to address. It's a very easy fix that can be done in this PR, but I wonder what the best approach would be.\r\n\r\nIMO, doppler should only be heard on a sound if both the emitter and listener have doppler enabled. That being said, this would require projects that use doppler and the camera as a listener to enable doppler on the camera, if they haven't already.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3043737168/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3100500156","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108051#issuecomment-3100500156","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108051","id":3100500156,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc64zeC8","user":{"login":"RoyBerardo","id":32561682,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTYxNjgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32561682?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo","html_url":"https://github.com/RoyBerardo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-22T02:20:44Z","updated_at":"2025-07-22T02:20:44Z","body":"Re-opening.\r\n\r\nFrom me in the past:\r\n> If doppler tracking is disabled on the listener but enabled on a stream player, doppler will still be heard.\r\n\r\nIMO this is fine. If it was the other way around, that would be a problem. Plus, this is how it's been for a while now anyways. I've updated the PR to add this info to the documentation. I'm not the greatest at writing docs, so I'd appreciate it if someone who is gave my updates a look :)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3100500156/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3104653575","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108051#issuecomment-3104653575","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108051","id":3104653575,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc65DUEH","user":{"login":"RoyBerardo","id":32561682,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTYxNjgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32561682?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo","html_url":"https://github.com/RoyBerardo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-22T19:57:53Z","updated_at":"2025-07-22T20:00:08Z","body":"@Calinou \r\n\r\nAh, this one is on me for not making an updated MRP for this PR :)\r\n\r\nThe MRP in the issue doesn't have saved settings for `doppler_tracking` on the listeners, since that property is introduced in this PR. Without setting `doppler_tracking`, listeners behave the same as master since the listener won't track its own velocity.\r\n\r\nI've attached an updated MRP to this comment, with `doppler_tracking` set on the listeners. \r\n[MRP_Fix_Test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21374313/MRP_Fix_Test.zip)\r\n\r\nVideo of the updated MRP:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/68f4a949-072e-4116-9722-f7638d79e15a\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3104653575/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3136529198","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108051#issuecomment-3136529198","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108051","id":3136529198,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6686Mu","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.co